# Database
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/lms?schema=public"

# NextAuth
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="your-secret-key-here"
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Upstash Redis (for rate limiting)
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL="https://your-redis-url.upstash.io"
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN="your-redis-token"

# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to .env
# 2. Generate a secure NEXTAUTH_SECRET: openssl rand -base64 32
# 3. Update DATABASE_URL with your actual database connection string
# 4. Update NEXTAUTH_URL to match your deployment URL
# 5. Create Upstash Redis database at https://console.upstash.com/
# 6. Copy Redis URL and token from Upstash console

# Vercel Deployment:
# 1. Add all environment variables in Vercel Dashboard:
#    - Go to Project Settings > Environment Variables
#    - Add each variable for Production, Preview, and Development environments
# 2. For NEXTAUTH_URL: Use your Vercel deployment URL (e.g., https://your-app.vercel.app)
# 3. For DATABASE_URL: Use Neon pooled connection string (recommended for serverless)
# 4. Database migrations: Run manually or use Neon's migration tool
#    - The postinstall script will generate Prisma client automatically during build